.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt MK.CONSTRAINTS.MK 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mk.constraints.mk
.Nd where a module or framework is built
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Evaluates
.Va PLATFORMS
and
.Va TOOLCHAINS
for the selected target, before any import or
.Va REQUIRES
is looked at, so an excluded module never fails on something only another
platform needs.
.Pp
Not included directly by a makefile.
.Ss Variables
Set in the module's or framework's makefile, before its
.Ic .include ;
both default to everything.
.Bl -tag -width "REASON.entry"
.It Va PLATFORMS
Systems, or system and architecture:
.Cm linux , linux_arm64 .
.It Va TOOLCHAINS
.Cm llvm , gcc , msvc .
.It Va REASON. Ns Ar entry
Text added to the message for that entry.
.El
.Pp
An entry is written:
.Bl -tag -width "!-name" -offset indent -compact
.It Ar name
only these; others are skipped quietly
.It Fl Ns Ar name
not these; skipped quietly
.It Cm \&! Ns Ar name
only these; anything else is an error
.It Cm \&!- Ns Ar name
not these; choosing one is an error
.El
.Pp
Plain and negative entries mix only when each negative is part of a plain entry,
such as
.Ql linux -linux_arm64 .
.Pp
A skip is intent, not failure: one line, exit 0, and
.Xr mk.skipped.mk 5
takes over.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
PLATFORMS=macos linux
TOOLCHAINS=!-gcc
REASON.gcc=miscompiles the raster kernels, use TOOLCHAIN=llvm
\&.include <mk.lib.mk>
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
Errors and warnings are not given for a
.Fl V
query,
.Cm clean
or
.Cm help :
asking about a build must not fail because of where it is not built.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mk.constraint-axis.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.framework.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.lib.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.prog.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.skipped.mk 5 ,
.Xr bmake-it 7
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Sylvain Souche
